# TouchDesigner vehicle — planned first, never started. The web builds took
# the model somewhere the original TD plan never went (real bathymetry, a
# shoreline), so this is parked rather than in progress. Ignored so a local
# .toe/.tox scratch dir doesn't imply work that isn't happening.
# The recon that was done is kept: docs/research/TD_IMPLEMENTATION.md.
td/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv*/
venv/

# Node — this repo deliberately has no dependencies; Playwright for the capture
# scripts is resolved from a sibling repo (see scripts/capture_presets.mjs).
node_modules/

# Local scratch and staging
.deploy/
scratch/
*.local

# Local state for an external tool, not part of this project. Ignored because
# the QA provenance stamp reads `git status` to decide whether a published
# snapshot was built from a dirty tree — an unrelated untracked directory was
# raising that banner on every build.
.embody/

# Raw OPeNDAP pull behind data/climatology/pp_cdip_climatology.json — 5 MB of
# CDIP hindcast, fully regenerable by rerunning build_cdip_climatology.py. The
# derived JSON is committed; the pull is not. Its SHA-256 is recorded in that
# JSON's source block so a rebuild is checkable without shipping the bytes.
data/climatology/.cache/

# Private working notes — outreach drafts, contact strategy, anything naming
# real people or unsent correspondence. This repo is public; nothing in here
# ships. Kept as a directory rather than loose files so there is one place to
# check before staging.
docs/drafts/

# ad-hoc review screenshots do not belong at the root (see docs/figures/ for
# generated, referenced figures)
/*.png

# QA contact sheets — HTML + ~125 PNGs regenerated in minutes by
# `node scripts/build_qa_sheets.mjs`. The generator is the artifact; the frames
# are not (commit b013197 removed 6.7 MB of unreferenced screenshots, and this
# is exactly the class of thing it removed).
# `qa/*` rather than `qa/` so ONE subdirectory can be re-included below (git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded).
qa/*
# Break-field instrument (scripts/measure_break_activation.mjs). The raw
# F(x,z) dumps (*.field.json, ~250 KB each) and run logs are regenerable in
# under a minute and stay ignored; the summary tables are the measurement the
# research note cites, so they are committed.
!qa/break-field/
qa/break-field/*
!qa/break-field/summary.json
# Signed reef-fit instrument (scripts/measure_reef_fit_signed.mjs): the beta
# scans, shape scans and station profiles regenerate in ~4 min and stay
# ignored; the report the research note cites is committed.
!qa/reef-fit-signed/
qa/reef-fit-signed/*
!qa/reef-fit-signed/report.md

# The tide axis of the peel floor (--mode=tide): one compact table per spot
# is the measurement TIDE_FLOOR_2026-09-01.md cites and is committed; the
# full (H0, tide) rungs grid beside it (~1 MB/spot) is regenerable and is not.
!qa/break-field/tide-floor/
qa/break-field/tide-floor/*.rungs.json

# Raw bathymetry pulls behind data/bathy/candidates/*/ — full CSMP zips and
# extracted 100-300 MB GeoTIFFs. Each candidate README records the URL, and the
# committed *_pp_clip.tif files are the spatial subsets the analysis reads.
data/bathy/candidates/*/raw/

# CSMP Aptos 2 m grid: null at every canon spot (the swath survey starts 325-565 m
# seaward of them), so the clip and its stage-frame JSON are a negative result kept
# out of history. candidates/csmp_aptos/README.md holds the recipe and the numbers.
data/bathy/candidates/csmp_aptos/*.tif
data/bathy/pp_bathy_csmp_aptos.json
# Reef-activation sensitivity (scripts/measure_reef_activation_sensitivity.mjs):
# same discipline as break-field — the summary is the measurement the research
# note cites and is committed; anything else the run drops there is not.
!qa/reef-activation/
qa/reef-activation/*
!qa/reef-activation/summary.json
